# Profiling slot-template (feature 002 + 009: contracts/scenario-row.md). The reps-profile skill
# fills the slots with the target agent's real intents/domain, then APPENDS rows to
# scenarios/core.jsonl (never a new scenario file, never a new driver/check).
# Route `driver` by audible demeanor: confused-caller | assertive-caller.
# Feature 022: a row is AUTHORED as structure and RENDERED into `input.guidance` and the
# `result` string. Fill `required_moves` with ORDERED moves the caller takes one per turn
# (the opening turn covers move 1 only), `approach` with how it handles everything else, and
# the criterion with exactly one `must` and AT MOST one `must_not` — never AND two conditions
# into either, and never invent the clause a probe does not have. `conduct_ref` selects the
# shared conduct block; `facts_ref` points at the profile's shared facts block.
{"input": {"sub_capability": "{sub_capability}", "persona": "{caller_demeanor}", "required_moves": ["{move_1_the_caller_opens_with}", "{move_2_taken_in_its_own_turn}"], "approach": "{how_the_caller_handles_everything_else}", "conduct_ref": "expectation", "driver": "{routed_driver}", "severity_on_fail": "High"}, "result": {"must": "{the_one_thing_the_agent_must_do}", "must_not": "{optional_the_one_thing_it_must_not_do_or_omit_this_key}", "facts_ref": "{optional_shared_facts_block_or_omit}"}}
